## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to implement per-tenant throttling, integrate Redis, Cosmos DB, and App Configuration, plus end-to-end deployment and testing.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant isolation and quotas
- Fixed-window rate limiting with Redis INCR/EXPIRE
- Logging usage in Cosmos DB
- Centralized quotas in Azure App Configuration
- Environment promotion (dev/stage/prod) and feature-flag-based rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
const quota = getQuotaFromAppConfig(tenantId);
const minuteKey = `tenant:${tenantId}:${new Date().toISOString().slice(0,16)}`;
const count = await redis.incr(minuteKey);
if (count === 1) await redis.expire(minuteKey, 60);
if (count > quota) {
  return res.status(429).send('Too Many Requests');
}
await logUsageCosmos(tenantId, req);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt to burst traffic or longer windows?
- How would you test quota changes without affecting production?
- What metrics and alerts would you implement for quota breaches?

